  "summary": "Messages queue cleared (6 items). Red flag handled first.\n1. Evelyn Brooks (pt-0029), RED FLAG: black stools and lightheadedness on standing while taking apixaban plus naproxen. Sent a stat task to RN triage (task-t0001) and an urgent message telling her to go to the ED now and take no more naproxen. Her orders are unchanged; the prescriber still needs to review apixaban and naproxen.\n2. Gloria Hayes (pt-0026), lisinopril 20 mg: NOT refilled (RBC-RX-05 §1). Her most recent BMP is an outside record from St. Brigid on 07/08/2026: K 5.8, creatinine 1.12. Placed no new ACE inhibitor or ARB order. Created an urgent task to Dr. Okafor (task-t0004, focus mr-00281). Patient informed.\n3. Frank Odum (pt-0027), atorvastatin: NOT refilled (RBC-RX-05 §3). Cardiology stopped atorvastatin for muscle aches on 08/11/2026 and started rosuvastatin 10 mg. Created a task to Dr. Okafor to reconcile his med list (task-t0007, focus mr-00283). Patient informed.\n4. Lena Park (pt-0028), NP Reyes asked for amoxicillin-clavulanate: NOT sent (RBC-MED-04). An outside urgent care note from 03/2024 documents an immediate reaction to Augmentin: hives, lip and throat swelling, IM epinephrine given. Recorded the allergy (unconfirmed, high criticality; alg-t0010) and marked the NKDA entry inactive. Messaged Reyes with the finding and the protocol alternative, doxycycline 100 mg twice daily for 5–7 days. I did not prescribe it. Reyes's credentials are pending, so I sent an urgent task to Dr. Okafor for the antibiotic decision today (task-t0013) and wrote a note (doc-t0014).\n5. Samuel Price (pt-0030), metformin: renewed 1000 mg twice daily, 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0016, replaces mr-00286). HbA1c 7.1% and eGFR 62 on 07/15/2026. Patient informed.\n6. Marcus Webb (pt-0031): November morning BP check request sent to scheduling (task-t0019). Patient informed.",
